  "theme": "curved",
  "mapLive": true,
  "_about": "After BMW's newer clusters (iDrive 8 / 8.5 Curved Display, Drive layout), generated by tools/gen_curved.py (edit that and regenerate): two thin bowed scales, speed left (SPEED_SCALE) and revs right (0..8), each with a band that lights from 0 to the needle in the drive mode's colour (theme 'curved' modes: blue Comfort, orange-red Sport, red Sport Plus, teal Eco Pro), the speed and range inside the left scale, the gear, the drive mode and the oil temperature inside the right one, a curved base line and a road to a soft horizon in the middle. While the Waze map shows inside the theme ('mapUp') the middle is cut see-through (mapLive: no rebuild). Everything that isn't text is one shader (cdash). The bottom row has the clock, coolant and outside temperature, BMW's gear letter left uncovered. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
